<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: GOLF-LEADING SCORES AT MEMORIAL AFTER FIRST ROUND.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING SCORES AT MEMORIAL AFTER FIRST ROUND.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN, Ohio 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores from the</p>
<p>$1.9 million Memorial Tournament after the first round on</p>
<p>Thursday at the 7,163 yard, par 72 course at Muirfield Village</p>
<p>G.C. (players U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>66 Tim Herron, Jesper Parnevik (Sweden), Glen Day, Billy</p>
<p>Andrade</p>
<p>67 Scott Hoch</p>
<p>68 Phil Blackmar, Guy Boros, Ernie Els (South Africa)</p>
<p>69 Don Pooley, Mike Standly, Jack Nicklaus, Andrew Magee,</p>
<p>Kelly Gibson, Billy Mayfair, Clarence Rose</p>
<p>70 Chris Perry, Kirk Triplett, Fred Funk, Tommy Tolles, Mark</p>
<p>O'Meara, Lee Janzen, Vijay Singh (Fiji), Davis Love</p>
<p>Add other non-U.S. scores</p>
<p>71 Greg Norman (Australia), Frank Nobilo (New Zealand)</p>
<p>72 David Frost (South Africa), Hideki Kase (Japan)</p>
<p>73 Peter Lonard (Australia), Craig Parry (Australia)</p>
<p>74 Shigeki Maruyama (Japan), Stuart Appleby (Australia),</p>
<p>Kazuhiko Hosokawa (Japan)</p>
<p>79 Fulton Allem (South Africa)</p>
<p>81 Warren Bladon (Britain)</p>
